      "created_at": "2016-12-17T18:06:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I remember having this discussion during playtesting with Naturalist way back when, and maybe I'm just remembering wrong, or maybe this is a change in the ruling. &nbsp;If I'm in Gazelle, and I play Bestial Shift, and use the bonus power to change to Rhino or Croc, then I also get their effect; no problem there. &nbsp;However, my memory is that even if you start in Croc, if you use the bonus power to change forms, you can \"go back\" and get the benefit of your new form. &nbsp;Essentially, the ruling was, \"the one-shot is still out, so you can still get those effects\". &nbsp;Like I said, it was widely discussed during playtesting, but that's the ruling I remember. &nbsp;However, in the game, it just goes strictly in order.</p><p>So, bug? &nbsp;Or did the ruling change? &nbsp;Or did I remember it wrong?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:31.851Z",
